      185.85,
      230.69,
      377.85,
      255.47
    ],
    "text": "AN ACT TO AMEND THE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDUREACT, NO. 15 OF 1979",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      270.89,
      401.9,
      295.67
    ],
    "text": "BE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      311.09,
      401.88,
      335.87
    ],
    "text": "1.This Act may be cited as the Code of CriminalProcedure (Amendment) Act, No. of 2016.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      351.29,
      401.9,
      402.83
    ],
    "text": "2.The following new section is hereby insertedimmediately after section 37 of the Code of CriminalProcedure Act, No. 15 of 1979 and shall have effect as section37A of that Code:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      215.85,
      418.25,
      401.91,
      523.43
    ],
    "text": "37A. (1) Any person who has beenarrested and detained in polic custody, shallhave the right to retain and consult anAttorney-at-law of his choice at his ownexpense, after the recording of his statementsin terms of the provisions of subsection (1) ofsection 110 and prior to being produced beforea Magistrate.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      215.85,
      538.85,
      401.9,
      670.79
    ],
    "text": "(2) If the person so arrested informs theofficer in-charge of the relevant police stationthat he is unable to retain and consult anAttorney-at-law at his own expense, the serviceof an Attorney-at-law from the Legal AidCommission of Sri Lanka established underthe Legal Aid Law, No. 27 of 1978, shall beprovided to him where the Legal AidCommission is in a position to provide suchservice.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      407.85,
      351.79,
      449.85,
      389.66
    ],
    "text": "Insertion ofsection 37Ain Act, No.15 of 1979.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
